# perf-viewer-main.qa (DESIGN §15.8, V-094): the viewer's frame time in the MAIN window, where the
# transcript shares the window with the 20,000-row list (perf-viewer.qa measures the viewer alone in
# a single-file window). Release `--features qa` build.
#
# Sandbox: a fresh copy of the template home, the synthetic corpus, the viewer fixtures, and the
# 3k-message perf transcript as a list row (UUID ffffffff-1c2d-4e5f-8a9b-0c1d2e3f4a5b):
#   tools/qa/new-sandbox.ps1 -Source <template home> -Dest <sbx>
#   tools/qa/add-synth-corpus.ps1 -Sandbox <sbx> -Count 20000
#   crates/gui/tests/fixtures/viewer/prepare-sandbox.ps1 -Sandbox <sbx>
#   tools/qa/add-perf-session.ps1 -Sandbox <sbx> -Source <sbx>\viewer\perf-3k.jsonl
# Run:
#   tools/qa/run-gui.ps1 -Sandbox <sbx> -Exe <release qa build> -Scenario crates/gui/qa/scenarios/perf-viewer-main.qa -Out <dir>
#
# Regression gate for the viewer's frame time in the shared window: render() start to paint end of
# the viewer, which in the main window spans the layout and paint of the whole window (the 20k-row
# list, the text-selection layer), not the viewer alone. Measured on the Windows dev machine in five
# runs (UI-thread CPU time ~ wall time, so it is real work, not load): idle median of nine re-renders
# 7.4-8.7 ms (single-file window: ~2 ms). That median is the gate (< 12 ms, ~1.4x the worst run): it
# catches a regression, it is not the 16.7 ms frame budget (the idle frame uses half of it; the open
# item in DESIGN §17.11 stays). The page-through (60 pages, last 100 frames) is reported, not asserted:
# on the shared desktop it varied too much to gate (avg 10.4-16.3 ms, p95 14.0-40.7 ms over five runs;
# one scheduler hiccup decides a p95). Medians judge, never one sampled frame.

wait-loaded 180s
expect list.total > 20000
paste "ffffffff-1c2d-4e5f-8a9b-0c1d2e3f4a5b"
wait-for list.count == 1 10s
key enter
wait-for viewer.status == ready 60s
expect viewer.messages > 2999
expect focus == viewer
wait 1500ms

# Idle frames: nine re-renders with nothing changed (SetToolsSummary while already Summary only notifies).
expect viewer.tool_display == sum
action history::SetToolsSummary
wait 150ms
action history::SetToolsSummary
wait 150ms
action history::SetToolsSummary
wait 150ms
action history::SetToolsSummary
wait 150ms
action history::SetToolsSummary
wait 150ms
action history::SetToolsSummary
wait 150ms
action history::SetToolsSummary
wait 150ms
action history::SetToolsSummary
wait 150ms
action history::SetToolsSummary
wait 150ms
timing viewer.frame_median_9 < 12ms
timing viewer.frame_cpu_median_9 >= 0

# Page-through: 60 pages, one frame each (reported).
key pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown
key pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown
key pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown
key pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown
key pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown
key pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown pagedown
timing viewer.frame_avg_100 >= 0
timing viewer.frame_p95_100 >= 0
quit 0
